WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Picture a great painted wheel.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:07.180
Six worlds turn around
it: gods, humans, animals,

3
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.360
hungry ghosts, and more.

4
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:15.170
At its centre sit three poisons:
greed, hatred and ignorance.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.470
Yet Buddhists teach that no
god sits above the wheel,

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.900
rewarding or punishing anyone.

7
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:25.990
So if no god is keeping score, why
should a Buddhist bother to be good?

8
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.670
In this mission, you'll find out
what Buddhists mean by kamma,

9
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.120
and why it is not the same as fate.

10
00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.730
Then you'll meet two qualities
at the heart of Buddhist ethics:

11
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.820
karuna and metta.

12
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.310
Your mission: find out why
Buddhists try to be good,

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.230
with no judge keeping score.
